## A4 vacuous-pass probe (fixtures under review-a-fixture)

- Fixture F1 (wrong content): apothecary row changed to `MAPS rating: 9.9` and
  `MAPS note: totally fabricated`. The checker PASSES 9/9, exit 0. The P1-c check
  tests field presence only, never value fidelity to the source record.
- Fixture F2 (wrong structure): watchtower row replaced by a warehouse duplicate,
  still 30 rows. The checker FAILS with 11 failures, exit 1. Slug coverage is real.
- Fixture F3 (wrong state): apothecary state cell `rated`. The checker FAILS with
  2 failures, exit 1. The state-cell parse is real.
- Empty or absent inventory: FAIL (red-p1.log, exit 1). Row count 0 fails `-eq 30`.

Conclusion: the checker cannot pass a missing or structurally wrong inventory, but
it can pass a wrong-content inventory (fabricated MAPS rating or note). The
committed inventory is faithful, so this is a checker-depth gap, not a defect in
the work.

